          %h2#categories_of_hypergraphs_definition Categories of hypergraphs: Definition
          %p
            As with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"}> graph
            ”, the word “hypergraph” does not have an entirely standardized meaning. We take as our starting point
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SchmidtStroehlein"} (Schmidt &amp; Ströhlein)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong category of simple hypergraphs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SimpHGrph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpHGrph
              has objects consisting of a pair of sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,E)
              equipped with a relation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi V
                      %mo ×
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \subseteq V \times E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi V
                    %mo ×
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ×
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R \subseteq V \times E) \to (R' \subseteq V' \times E')
              consisting of pairs of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f : V \to V', g : E \to E')
              which preserve the relation, i.e., such that for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\in V, e \in E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v,e) \in R
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mi v
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f v,g e) \in R'
          %p
            The category of simple hypergraphs could also be referred to more dryly as “the category of binary relations”, although this has potential for confusion with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
            (whose
            %em morphisms
            are binary relations).
          %p In a simple hypergraph, a hypervertex can be incident to a hyperedge at most once, but in some situations one wants to allow a hypervertex to be incident to a hyperedge multiple times. To define hypergraphs in this more general sense, we keep the intuition of hypergraphs-as-heterogenous-relations, but generalize relations to spans.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong category of hypergraphs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi HGrph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HGrph
              has objects consisting of a pair of sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,E)
              equipped with a span
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi v
                      %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi e
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \overset{v}\leftarrow R \overset{e}\rightarrow E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi v
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi e
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ′
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V \overset{v}\leftarrow R \overset{e}\rightarrow E) \to (V' \overset{v'}\leftarrow R' \overset{e'}\rightarrow E')
              consisting of triples of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f : V \to V', g : E \to E', h:R \to R')
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v'\circ h = f\circ v
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi h
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e'\circ h = g\circ e
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi HGrph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HGrph
            is just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            over the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"} walking
            cospan”
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mo •
                    %mo ←
                    %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet \rightarrow \bullet \leftarrow \bullet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SimpHGrph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpHGrph
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi HGrph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HGrph
          %h2#hypergraphs_from_a_topostheoretic_perspective Hypergraphs from a topos-theoretic perspective
          %p
            In Lawvere (
            %a{:href => "#Law86"} 1986
            p.6,
            %a{:href => "#Law89"} 1989
            pp.283-4) it is pointed out that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+topos"} spatial topos
            since it is equivalent to the topos of sheaves on the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=\{a,b,c\}
            with topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau=\{\emptyset,\{a\},\{b\},\{a,b\},\{a,b,c\}\}
            i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has two isolated points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/focal+point"} focal
            one
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            whose only neighborhood is the whole space.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+subtoposes"} lattice of subtoposes
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
            consists (besides the two obvious subtoposes) of one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subtopos"} closed
            and two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open
            copies of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+topos"} Sierpinski topos
            complementing the open copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            respectively and an open
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\times Set=Sh(\{a,b\})=Sh_{\neg\neg}(Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet})
            complementing the closed copy of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattered+topos"} scattered topos
          %p
            The complementary open-closed pairs of the subtopos lattice correspond precisely to analyses of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+gluing"} Artin gluing
          %p
            For instance, take the product functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcap\colon Set\times Set\to Set
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Y)\mapsto X\times  Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcap
            is left exact since it forms an adjoint string with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+functor"} diagonal functor
            and the coproduct functor:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ▵
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ⊓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcup\dashv \triangle\dashv\sqcap
            \.
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)
            has objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((X,Y),Z, u\colon Z\to X\times Y)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Y)\in Set\times Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z\in Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            is a morphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Z
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon Z\overset{\langle u_0, u_1\rangle}{\rightarrow} X\times Y
            corresponds to a pair of maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)
            really correspond to spans in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            The open inclusion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\times Set
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\ast \colon Set\times Set\to \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap) \qquad (X,Y)\mapsto ((X,Y),X\times Y,id_{X\times Y})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast\colon \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)\to Set\times Set \qquad ((X,Y),Z,u)\mapsto (X,Y)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_{!} \colon Set\times Set\to \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap) \qquad (X,Y)\mapsto ((X,Y),0,0\to X\times Y) \quad ,
          %p
            and the closed inclusion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\ast \colon Set\to \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap) \qquad X\mapsto ((1,1),X,X\to 1\times 1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Z
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\ast\colon\mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)\to Set \qquad ((X,Y),Z,u)\mapsto Z\quad .
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ▵
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ⊓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle\dashv\sqcap
            the closed inclusion is
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!\colon Set \to \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)\qquad X\mapsto ((X,X), X,  X\overset{\langle id_X,id_X\rangle}{\to} X\times X)\quad .
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ▵
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcup\dashv \triangle
            there is a somewhat surprising further left adjoint:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi u
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\circ\colon\mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)\to Set \qquad ((X,Y),Z,u)\mapsto X\sqcup_u Y\quad .
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi u
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\sqcup_u Y
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 0
                  %mi Z
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 1
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\overset{u_0}{\leftarrow} Z\overset{u_1}{\rightarrow} Y
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1
            are the pair of maps provided by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Z
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon Z\overset{\langle u_0, u_1\rangle}{\rightarrow} X\times Y
            \. Since a map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((X,Y),Z,u)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!(W)
            is a triple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_0,f_1,f_2)
            such that the following diagram commutes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                              %msub
                                %mi u
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi u
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi W
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo ×
                          %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Z &amp; \overset{\langle u_0, u_1\rangle}{\rightarrow} &amp; X\times Y
                  \\\
                  f_2\downarrow &amp;  &amp;f_0\downarrow \downarrow f_1
                  \\\
                  W &amp; \overset{\langle id_W, id_W\rangle}{\rightarrow} &amp; W\times W
                  }
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_0,f_1,f_2)
            has to satisfy the two conditions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0 u_0= f_2
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 u_1=f_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0 u_0=f_1 u_1
            \. But this is the same as giving a map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi u
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\circ ((X,Y),Z,u)= X\sqcup_u Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            by the universal property of the pushout.
          %p Whence we get an adjoint string:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔾𝕝
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\circ\dashv j_!\dashv j^\ast \dashv j_\ast \colon Set\to \mathbb{Gl}(\sqcap)
          %p
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\ast
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Gl}(\sqcap)
            almost as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
            is spatial it is not expected to satisfy all of Lawvere’s axioms. In particular, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nullstellensatz"} Nullstellensatz
            is violated since none of the copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ←
                        %mo •
                        %mo →
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            be the diagram category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi t
                    %mi s
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\overset{s}{\underset{t}{\rightrightarrows}} A
            underlying the topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Q
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Q^{op}}
            of directed graphs or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quivers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            of the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            into the presheaves:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(A)=Hom_Q(-,A)
            = succeed "rrow" do
              %em a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_2=\bullet\to\bullet
            , the other basic figure being the
            = succeed "ode" do
              %em n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(N)
            \.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Q
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_Q Y(A)
            is just the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mo •
                  %mo ←
                  %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet\rightarrow \bullet\leftarrow\bullet
            underlying the hypergraphs. Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(A)
            is the representable presheaf corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            this is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q/A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Q
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Q^{op}}
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tendue"} étendue topos
            using a general formula for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slices
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf toposes
            and suggesting to view a quiver as a ‘foliated’ hypergraph:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Q
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi Q
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ←
                      %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Q^{op}}/Y(A)\simeq Set^{(Q/A)^{op}}\simeq Set^{(\int_Q Y(A))^{op}}\simeq Set^{\bullet\leftarrow\bullet\rightarrow\bullet}\quad .
          %p This equivalence will be further explained in terms of graph colorings in the next section.
          %h2#hypergraphs_as_2colored_graphs Hypergraphs as 2-colored graphs
          %p
            There is a classical equivalence between hypergraphs and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+coloring"} 2-colored
            (hence
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bipartite+graph"} bipartite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(H)
            whose vertex set is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of the hypervertices and the hyperedges of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi v
                  %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_v \sim x_e
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(H)
            whenever the corresponding pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v,e)
            are incident in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            (creating multiple edges in the case of multiple incidence). By coloring vertices corresponding to hypervertices in black and vertices corresponding to hyperedges in white, we satisfy the requirement that no pair of vertices sharing an edge have the same color. Conversely, this construction is clearly reversible: any 2-colored graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            determines a hypergraph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(G)
            by interpreting black vertices as hypervertices and white vertices as hyperedges that connect all of their (black vertex) neighbors.
          %p
            Giving a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+coloring"} vertex coloring
            of a graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            colors is equivalent to building a graph homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to K_n
            into the complete graph on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            vertices, and so graphs equipped with a
            = succeed "-coloring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice"} slice
            category over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi HGrph
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Grph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HGrph \cong Grph/K_2
          %p
            between the category of hypergraphs and the slice over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_2
            of the category of graphs, where by the latter we mean “pseudographs” in the greatest level of generality, allowing for loops, multiple edges between vertices, and dangling half-edges (as described in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph#definition_in_terms_of_action_on_a_set_of_halfedges"} this definition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SimpHGrph
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi LoopGrph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpHGrph \cong LoopGrph/K_2
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LoopGraph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LoopGraph
            is the category of “loop graphs”, i.e., the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Grph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grph
            whose objects are symmetric relations.
